089 :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}, \\mathbf{a}_{2}, \\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nII. $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$.\n\nIII. $-\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$." "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [:db/cas 17592186707089 :question/worked-solution "A set is **linearly independent** when the equation $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$. A nontrivial solution proves **linear dependence**.\n\nTest the proposed combination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}&=-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous vector equation gives the coordinate system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x_{1}+x_{3} &=0 \\\\ -x_{1}-x_{2} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nChoose one coefficient nonzero and solve the remaining coordinate equations by substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_{1}&=1 \\\\ -2(1)+x_{3}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{3}=2 \\\\ -(1)-x_{2}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{2}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives a nontrivial solution. Verify it directly:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}-\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nThe coefficients are not all zero, so the set is **linearly dependent**.\n\nStatement I is **true**. Statement II is **false**. Statement III is **true**." "A set is **linearly independent** when the equation $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$. A nontrivial solution proves **linear dependence**.\n\nTest the proposed combination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}&=-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous vector equation gives the coordinate system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x_{1}+x_{3} &=0 \\\\ -x_{1}-x_{2} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nChoose one coefficient nonzero and solve the remaining coordinate equations by substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_{1}&=1 \\\\ -2(1)+x_{3}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{3}=2 \\\\ -(1)-x_{2}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{2}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives a nontrivial solution. Verify it directly:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}-\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nThe coefficients are not all zero, so the set is **linearly dependent**.\n\nThe statement “The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}, \\mathbf{a}_{2}, \\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent.” is **true**. The statement “$x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$.” is **false**. The statement “$-\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$.” is **true**."] [:db/ensure 17592186707089 :question/validate] {:db/id "17592186564487-I-false" :answer/id #uuid "840cced0-091d-5c36-a464-3bbbc9bb770d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-I-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186564487-I-true" :answer/id #uuid "350f121c-4cc1-591f-973e-b1397acfed86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-I-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186564487-I" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1daec68-4dca-515c-9d3e-674467fb12ef" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186564487-I-false" "17592186564487-I-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186564487-I-false"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-I" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186564487 :question/answer-fields "17592186564487-I"] {:db/id "17592186564487-II-false" :answer/id #uuid "7e58883b-f950-576c-9537-17cb8cc83d90" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-II-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186564487-II-true" :answer/id #uuid "1dbcdd93-9c6d-5bc2-9254-d4719b9b0362" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-II-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186564487-II" :answer-field/id #uuid "137c78ef-e711-5be3-b357-7e936b53f5d5" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186564487-II-false" "17592186564487-II-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186564487-II-true"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-II" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186564487 :question/answer-fields "17592186564487-II"] {:db/id "17592186564487-III-false" :answer/id #uuid "536c2f80-0a4c-5357-8ad2-e854ca1ffa65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-III-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186564487-III-true" :answer/id #uuid "22338f84-167c-5025-8423-2585708b4881" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-III-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186564487-III" :answer-field/id #uuid "d21b5157-4d73-5a18-a475-ef8977bd17e2" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solution." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186564487-III-false" "17592186564487-III-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186564487-III-false"} [:db/ensure "17592186564487-III" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186564487 :question/answer-fields "17592186564487-III"] [:db/retract 17592186564487 :question/answer-fields 17592186564381] [:db/cas 17592186564487 :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 20 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nII. The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nIII. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solution." "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 20 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [:db/cas 17592186564487 :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+20{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-13{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 20 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(\\mathbf{0})+9(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$, we get that the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true." "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+20{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-13{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 20 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(\\mathbf{0})+9(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$, we get that the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the statements “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.” and “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solution.” are false, while the statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent.” is true."] [:db/ensure 17592186564487 :question/validate] {:db/id "17592186706984-I-false" :answer/id #uuid "29d2f8b9-7717-5b2a-bab7-0e2150a73629" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-I-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706984-I-true" :answer/id #uuid "74a2873d-3b33-5497-8aba-e5fb210830d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-I-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706984-I" :answer-field/id #uuid "70ce502f-3100-564c-8bd3-c6b1aecb01d3" :answer-field/key "The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186706984-I-false" "17592186706984-I-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186706984-I-true"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-I" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186706984 :question/answer-fields "17592186706984-I"] {:db/id "17592186706984-II-false" :answer/id #uuid "c2f2f17c-7100-5686-98fd-9bcda0501d01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-II-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706984-II-true" :answer/id #uuid "4fbd0175-9929-5207-884a-82d2aebee61c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-II-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706984-II" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d5a9a80-dcc1-5b98-aa1b-ebe9bb814307" :answer-field/key "The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186706984-II-false" "17592186706984-II-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186706984-II-false"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-II" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186706984 :question/answer-fields "17592186706984-II"] {:db/id "17592186706984-III-false" :answer/id #uuid "fdc5480d-1570-58ea-a35d-cf9d828d5c9b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-III-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706984-III-true" :answer/id #uuid "b9fe2c93-6477-5b26-b833-2b69187d9a99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-III-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706984-III" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d5e56dd-b3ca-536f-b0cb-6dc4b546e576" :answer-field/key "The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions with coefficients not all zero." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186706984-III-false" "17592186706984-III-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186706984-III-false"} [:db/ensure "17592186706984-III" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186706984 :question/answer-fields "17592186706984-III"] [:db/retract 17592186706984 :question/answer-fields 17592186706993] [:db/cas 17592186706984 :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_3=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFor real $x_1,x_2,x_3$, use row reduction to analyze $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$. Which statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent.\n\nII. The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent.\n\nIII. The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions with coefficients not all zero.\n\nChoose the correct combination." "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_3=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFor real $x_1,x_2,x_3$, use row reduction to analyze $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$. Which statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [:db/cas 17592186706984 :question/worked-solution "Place the three vectors in the columns of the coefficient matrix. The homogeneous equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_1-x_2-2x_3 &=0 \\\\ x_1-x_3 &=0 \\\\ 2x_1-x_3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAppend the zero right-hand side and use the following row operations in order.\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are $1,2,3$. Back substitution, beginning with the last row, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_3=0 \\\\ x_2+x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_2=0 \\\\ x_1-x_2-2x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $x_1=x_2=x_3=0$ is the only solution. The vectors are **linearly independent**; there is no nontrivial solution and no free variable.\n\nI is true. II is false. III is false. Choose “I only”." "Place the three vectors in the columns of the coefficient matrix. The homogeneous equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_1-x_2-2x_3 &=0 \\\\ x_1-x_3 &=0 \\\\ 2x_1-x_3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAppend the zero right-hand side and use the following row operations in order.\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are $1,2,3$. Back substitution, beginning with the last row, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_3=0 \\\\ x_2+x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_2=0 \\\\ x_1-x_2-2x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $x_1=x_2=x_3=0$ is the only solution. The vectors are **linearly independent**; there is no nontrivial solution and no free variable.\n\nThe statement “The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent.” is true. The statement “The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent.” is false. The statement “The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions with coefficients not all zero.” is false."] [:db/ensure 17592186706984 :question/validate] {:db/id "17592186706986-I-false" :answer/id #uuid "5d7023dd-b727-5cec-8663-e90859af7196" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false"} [:db/ensure "17592186706986-I-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706986-I-true" :answer/id #uuid "62de5a26-bed0-5987-813a-18724f66a3cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186706986-I-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706986-I" :answer-field/id #uuid "f565f186-f27a-5822-8a13-fc268804d07d" :answer-field/key "The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186706986-I-false" "17592186706986-I-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186706986-I-false"} [:db/ensure "17592186706986-I" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186706986 :question/answer-fields "17592186706986-I"] {:db/id "17592186706986-II-false" :answer/id #uuid "e35adf39-dea9-586e-b5d6-3e20db757dcd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false"} [:db/ensure "17592186706986-II-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706986-II-true" :answer/id #uuid "2941ec88-9d83-5713-aee4-358122903e92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186706986-II-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186706986-II" :answer-field/id #uuid "028a078a-a19e-5ec0-852d-61840b8ca09b" :answer-field/key "The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186706986-II-false" "17592186706986-II-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186706986-II-true"} [:db/ensure "17592186706986-II" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186706986 :question/answer-fields "17592186706986-II"] {:db/id "175