_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$. Its augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nCarry out these operations in the order shown: $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-R_1$; then $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_1$; then $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_2$. Use the resulting pivots and free variables to decide which statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [:db/cas 17592186707030 :question/worked-solution "Place the three vectors in the columns of the coefficient matrix. The homogeneous equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_1+2x_2-x_3 &=0 \\\\ x_1+3x_2+x_3 &=0 \\\\ 2x_1+6x_2+2x_3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAppend the zero right-hand side and use the following row operations in order.\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are $1,2$. The variable $x_3$ is free. Set $x_3=t$ and back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_3&=t \\\\ x_2+2x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_2=-2t \\\\ x_1+2x_2-x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1=5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n(x_1,x_2,x_3)=(5t,-2t,t),\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nFor every $t\\ne0$, the coefficients are not all zero. Therefore there are infinitely many nontrivial solutions, and the vectors are **linearly dependent**. A zero final row imposes no additional constraint.\n\nI is true. II is false. III is true. Choose “I and III only”." "Place the three vectors in the columns of the coefficient matrix. The homogeneous equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_1+2x_2-x_3 &=0 \\\\ x_1+3x_2+x_3 &=0 \\\\ 2x_1+6x_2+2x_3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAppend the zero right-hand side and use the following row operations in order.\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are $1,2$. The variable $x_3$ is free. Set $x_3=t$ and back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_3&=t \\\\ x_2+2x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_2=-2t \\\\ x_1+2x_2-x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1=5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n(x_1,x_2,x_3)=(5t,-2t,t),\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nFor every $t\\ne0$, the coefficients are not all zero. Therefore there are infinitely many nontrivial solutions, and the vectors are **linearly dependent**. A zero final row imposes no additional constraint.\n\nThe statement “The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions with coefficients not all zero.” is true. The statement “The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_1=x_2=x_3=0$.” is false. The statement “The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent.” is true."] [:db/ensure 17592186707030 :question/validate] {:db/id "17