7592186707038-III-false" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186707038-III-true" :answer/id #uuid "f8c68811-8301-5c8c-9163-58a0e65ec94e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true"} [:db/ensure "17592186707038-III-true" :answer/validate] {:db/id "17592186707038-III" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a5cd3ca-1f74-57de-bc64-fec6dfb43d49" :answer-field/key "The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox :answer-field/choices ["17592186707038-III-false" "17592186707038-III-true"] :answer-field/correct "17592186707038-III-false"} [:db/ensure "17592186707038-III" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186707038 :question/answer-fields "17592186707038-III"] [:db/retract 17592186707038 :question/answer-fields 17592186707052] [:db/cas 17592186707038 :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_3=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFor real $x_1,x_2,x_3$, form the equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$. Its augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nCarry out these operations in the order shown: $R_2\\leftarrow R_2+2R_1$; then $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+R_1$; then $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+2R_2$. Use the resulting pivots and free variables to decide which statements are true.\n\nI. The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions with coefficients not all zero.\n\nII. The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_1=x_2=x_3=0$.\n\nIII. The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent.\n\nChoose the correct combination." "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_3=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFor real $x_1,x_2,x_3$, form the equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$. Its augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nCarry out these operations in the order shown: $R_2\\leftarrow R_2+2R_1$; then $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+R_1$; then $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+2R_2$. Use the resulting pivots and free variables to decide which statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [:db/cas 17592186707038 :question/worked-solution "Place the three vectors in the columns of the coefficient matrix. The homogeneous equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_1-2x_2+x_3 &=0 \\\\ -2x_1+5x_2-x_3 &=0 \\\\ -x_1-5x_3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAppend the zero right-hand side and use the following row operations in order.\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2+2R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+2R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are $1,2,3$. Back substitution, beginning with the last row, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_3=0 \\\\ x_2+x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_2=0 \\\\ x_1-2x_2+x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $x_1=x_2=x_3=0$ is the only solution. The vectors are **linearly independent**; there is no nontrivial solution and no free variable.\n\nI is false. II is true. III is false. Choose “II only”." "Place the three vectors in the columns of the coefficient matrix. The homogeneous equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_1-2x_2+x_3 &=0 \\\\ -2x_1+5x_2-x_3 &=0 \\\\ -x_1-5x_3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAppend the zero right-hand side and use the following row operations in order.\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2+2R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+2R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are $1,2,3$. Back substitution, beginning with the last row, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_3=0 \\\\ x_2+x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_2=0 \\\\ x_1-2x_2+x_3&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $x_1=x_2=x_3=0$ is the only solution. The vectors are **linearly independent**; there is no nontrivial solution and no free variable.\n\nThe statement “The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions with coefficients not all zero.” is false. The statement “The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_1=x_2=x_3=0$.” is true. The statement “The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent.” is false."] [:db/ensu